_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, for each repository-facing cluster (_retire, note_absent_or_rekey, record_comment_id, unretire), which side owns save()/alert()/save_retired()/retired_entries() after extraction and pin the retired-first-then-live ordering, so the owner-vs-facade split does not alter the sequencing AC1-AC3 preserve.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5487,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 3: 'Use open typed views over the same dictionaries. Unknown and legacy fields remain present and writable only through named policy operations.'","Plan step 2: 'the facade... coordinates the lifecycle owner and repository unit-of-work; no adapter or reconciler caller receives a writable repository object.'","Code: binding_store.py _retire (L508-538) writes retired FIRST via self._repo.save_retired(retired_entries), then pops live bindings/reverse, then self.save(), then self._repo.alert(...) — a stated crash-safety ordering invariant.","Code: note_absent_or_rekey (L491-506) mutates dicts then self.save() then self._repo.alert('binding-rekeyed'); record_comment_id (L406-410) calls self.save() immediately; unretire (L598-615) calls self._repo.retired_entries()/save_retired()/alert().","ABSENCE: plan text does not name the owner of save()/alert()/save_retired()/retired_entries() after the move, nor pin the retired-first-then-live ordering that AC2 (retirement) and AC3 (tombstone/alert) depend on."],"finding":"Several clusters the plan extracts into binding_lifecycle.py are not pure dictionary mutations — _retire, note_absent_or_rekey, record_comment_id, and unretire perform repository-facing side effects (self.save(), self._repo.alert(...), self._repo.save_retired(...), self._repo.retired_entries()), yet the plan describes the owner as 'operating on the repository original dictionaries' via 'open typed views' and does not state which side (lifecycle owner vs facade) owns those save/alert/save_retired emissions or their ordering relative to the dict mutation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faba16a4dce0dfaf6","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 1-3; AC1-AC3","norm_id":"nf829d46d20a417c5","priority":0.2513,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer moves _retire into the owner and either duplicates the repository handle there (violating the spirit of step 2's writable-repository constraint) or leaves save/alert in the facade, splitting the retired-first-then-live ordering across two modules and reopening the crash window.","The 'binding-rekeyed' save+alert sequence in note_absent_or_rekey ends up on the facade side while the dict re-key happens in the owner, so a partial move changes when the durable save lands relative to the reverse-index swap."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a plan line specifying that the lifecycle owner returns/decides the dict transition while the FACADE retains the save()/alert()/save_retired() calls (keeping the repository unit-of-work solely on the facade), and that the retired-first-then-live-drop ordering in _retire and the save-then-alert ordering in rekey/unretire are reproduced unchanged.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_